course: dictionary
lesson: 7990
title: The rectangle
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A rectangle is a flat shape with four straight sides and four square corners, called right angles. Opposite sides are equal and parallel, so it has a long side (length) and a short side (width).
explain: «The perimeter of a rectangle is twice the length plus twice the width.» Perimeter means the distance all the way round the outside. You can add all four sides, or use the short cut: add the length and width, then double the answer.
explain: «For example, a plan of your room drawn at a scale of 1 to 50 shows a 2-metre bed as a rectangle 4 centimetres long.» A scale tells you how real lengths shrink on a drawing. Here 1 centimetre on the plan stands for 50 centimetres, so 200 cm ÷ 50 = 4 cm.
explain: A square is a special rectangle where all four sides are equal. Every square is a rectangle, but not every rectangle is a square.
fact: A rectangle has four sides and four right angles.
fact: The area of a rectangle is length × width, measured in square units such as square metres.
fact: «Cut it into two rectangles instead, 10 by 5 and 6 by 3: 50 + 18 = 68, the same.» You can split a shape into rectangles, find each area, and add them up.
fact: Doors, books, phone screens and tables are everyday rectangles.
exercise: How many right angles does a rectangle have? | Six | Two | Three | *Four
exercise: What is the length plus the width of a rectangle that is 6 cm long and 3 cm wide? | *9 cm | 3 cm | 18 cm | 12 cm
exercise: Which special rectangle has all four sides equal? | Circle | Triangle | *Square | Pentagon
test: A rectangle is 10 cm by 5 cm. What is its area? | 100 square cm | 30 cm | *50 square cm | 15 square cm
test: On a plan drawn at a scale of 1 to 50, a 2-metre bed is drawn how long? | 200 cm | 2 cm | *4 cm | 40 cm
exam: «A 10 m by 8 m rectangle with a 4 m by 3 m corner cut out has 10 × 8 - 4 × 3 = 80 - 12 = 68 square metres.» What is the area left after the corner is cut out? | *68 square metres | 80 square metres | 92 square metres | 12 square metres
